            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "## Steps"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "1. [P1] Read the request in your prompt: its inputs, every acceptance criterion and the deliverable. The criteria come from the contract and can only be met, never changed; copy the relevant ones verbatim into every task you delegate."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "2. [P2] Delegate to `writer` (Writer) with `budget=3`: its part of the request, with the criteria it must meet."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "3. [P3] Read the final artifact yourself and check it against EVERY criterion of the request, quoting counts from your own `read` output."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "4. [P4] Report: `done` only if every criterion is met (else `blocked` with the deviation and a recommended decision). Name the deliverable's path (the assistant copies it to /private/tmp/hirearchy-p2/R1-1793275867/deliverables) and pass `lessons` as an after-action review: Expected / Happened / Caught at / Cause / Prevent (the system cause, not a person), or Near miss when nothing went wrong."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "## Budget plan"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "- [P5] Request budget: 8 runs (the contract's). Hand down no more than this up front, each with `budget=` set explicitly:"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "- [P6] writer: 3 runs (2 work + 1 rework or re-check)"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "- [P7] you (lead): keep 5 runs: your own 5 (plan, process each result, final check, report, one rework cycle)."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "Unspent runs return to your parent with your final report."
            }
          ],
